# The shared lines, Phase 8 session 2 (Docs/Design/84 §33.1, §33.3): the answers a question makes due when no concept's
# own rule answers it: how one is (answer.how and its variants), what one means to do (answer.plan), where one's been
# or going (answer.whereabouts), what ails one (answer.check_in), what one said (clarify); and the turns around a
# closing and an apology: one more thing before parting (extend), and an apology not taken (decline_apology). Move
# lines (no concept).
#
# An answer about oneself is true to the speaker's own facts: well only when nothing ails them, hungry when hungry,
# busy at work, grieving when mourning; where the facts say nothing, the ordinary deflections ("Getting by."). A
# question of where may be "where've you been?" or "where are you off to?", so the answers fit both. An extend is
# seldom (it weighs little beside taking the leave), and an apology is seldom refused.

## answer.how: how one is

rule s8a_how_any
does answer.how.deflect
say #s8_fine# | #s8_fine# | #fine#. | Oh, you know. | Same as ever. | Getting by.

rule s8a_how_any2
does answer.how.deflect
say Not so bad. | Still here. | Can't grumble, or I'd never stop. | One day at a time. | Mustn't complain.

rule s8a_how_well
does answer.how.well
when self.mood=bright|even self.hungry!=yes self.injured!=light|bad self.mourning!=kin|friend
say Well, thank you. | Good, thanks. Busy, but good. | Very well, as it happens. | Can't complain. Truly. | All the better for asking.

rule s8a_how_bright
does answer.how.well
when self.mood=bright self.hungry!=yes self.mourning!=kin|friend
tone light
say Never better. | Grand, thank you. Grand. | Happy as a lark. | On top of the world, today.

rule s8a_how_newborn
does answer.how.well
when self.mood_why=newborn
tone light
say Tired and happy. There's a new pup at ours. | Short of sleep, but I'd not change it. | Over the moon, if you must know.

rule s8a_how_wed
does answer.how.well
when self.mood_why=wed
tone light
say Still getting used to being wed. | Happy. Is that allowed? | Never better, since the wedding.

rule s8a_how_trade
does answer.how.well
when self.mood_why=trade self.hungry!=yes
say Business is good, so I'm good. | Busy, and the till's full. Can't ask more. | Doing well, touch wood.

rule s8a_how_hungry
does answer.how.poorly
when self.hungry=yes
say Hungry, if I'm honest. | Lean. The belly's empty more than it's full. | I've had better weeks. Hungrier ones too. | Empty, mostly.

rule s8a_how_hurt
does answer.how.poorly
when self.injured=light|bad
say Sore. I took a knock. | Stiff, and slow with it. | Mending, slowly. | I've been better. It'll heal.

rule s8a_how_low
does answer.how.poorly
when self.mood=low self.mourning!=kin|friend
say Not so good, truth be told. | Low. I don't know why. | A bit down, that's all. | I've been better.

rule s8a_how_sore
does answer.how.poorly
when self.mood=sore
say Out of sorts. Don't ask. | Cross, if you want the truth. | Sore about something. It'll pass.

rule s8a_how_robbed
does answer.how.poorly
when self.mood_why=robbed
say Robbed, and still cross about it. | Poorer than I was, thanks to some thief. | Not good. I was robbed, you know.

rule s8a_how_busy
does answer.how.busy
when self.working=yes
say #bc_very_busy# | Busy. No rest for anyone. | Up to my ears. | Run ragged, but there it is. | Busy as ever.

rule s8a_how_grieving
does answer.how.grieving
when self.mourning=kin|friend
tone tender
say I'm up and about. That's something. | Getting through the days. | Some mornings are hard. | It's the quiet I mind. That's all. | Better for the company.

rule s8a_how_homeless
does answer.how.poorly
when self.homeless=yes
say Rough, mostly. | Looking for a dry corner, same as ever. | Still without a roof, if you're asking.

## answer.plan: what one means to do

rule s8a_plan_any
does answer.plan
say #planless#. | Oh, the usual. | Nothing much. | Haven't decided. | #bc_we_will_see# | Whatever comes.

rule s8a_plan_work_before
does answer.plan
when self.working=yes self.shift=before
say Work, and soon. | Off to work in a bit. | The usual. A day's work. | Work first. Then we'll see.

rule s8a_plan_work_during
does answer.plan
when self.working=yes self.shift=during
say Finish this, then home. | Get through the day, mostly. | Work till it's done. | Back to it, after this.

rule s8a_plan_work_after
does answer.plan
when self.shift=after
say Home, and my feet up. | Supper, and an early night. | Nothing. I've earned it. | Rest, if anyone lets me.

rule s8a_plan_day_off
does answer.plan
when self.shift=day_off here.time=dawn|day
say Nothing, if I can help it. | A day to myself, for once. | I mean to enjoy it. | Odd jobs about the place.

rule s8a_plan_night
does answer.plan
when here.time=night
say Bed, and soon. | Sleep, if my head lets me. | Home. It's late. | Nothing but my bed.

rule s8a_plan_festival
does answer.plan
when world.festival=today|soon
tone light
say The festival, like everyone. | Dancing, if my feet hold out. | Eat too much, I expect. | I'll be at the festival.

rule s8a_plan_rest
does answer.plan
when here.day=rest
say Chapel, then supper. | It's Restday. Nothing. | Rest, as the day says. | Sit in the sun, if there is any.

rule s8a_plan_young
does answer.plan
when self.stage=young
tone light
say Playing! | Find the others. | I'm going to the water! | Climb something. | Explore!

rule s8a_plan_teen
does answer.plan
when self.stage=adolescent
say #bc_nothing# | Get out of chores. | Dunno. Something. | Find the others, maybe.

rule s8a_plan_farm
does answer.plan
when self.job=farmer|herder
say Out to the fields. | The beasts want seeing to. | Fences, and more fences. | Whatever the land wants of me.

rule s8a_plan_water
does answer.plan
when self.job=fisher|sailor
say Out on the water, weather allowing. | Nets to mend first. | Whatever the tide says.

rule s8a_plan_shop
does answer.plan
when self.job=merchant|baker|brewer|innkeeper|cook
say Open up and sell what I can. | Keep the shop. Same as always. | Count the stock, curse the prices.

rule s8a_plan_hungry
does answer.plan
when self.hungry=yes
say Find something to eat, first. | Eat, if I can. | Food. Then the rest.

rule s8a_plan_homeless
does answer.plan
when self.homeless=yes
say Find somewhere dry to sleep. | Keep out of the wind. | Same as every day. Get by.

## answer.whereabouts: where one's been, or going (the answers fit both)

rule s8a_where_any
does answer.whereabouts
say Oh, here and there. | About my business. | Nowhere much. | Just about. | Here, there. You know.

rule s8a_where_work
does answer.whereabouts
when self.job!=none|child|beggar self.stage=adult|old
say Work, mostly. | Where the work is. | At it, same as ever.

rule s8a_where_home
does answer.whereabouts
when self.homeless=no
say Home, mostly. | Between home and work. | Not far from my own door.

rule s8a_where_young
does answer.whereabouts
when self.stage=young|adolescent
say Nowhere! | Just out. | Around. | With the others.

## answer.check_in: what ails one

rule s8a_checkin_any
does answer.check_in
say I'm all right, really. | Nothing a sit-down won't fix. | Oh, it's nothing. | I'll live. | Don't fuss. I'm fine.

rule s8a_checkin_tired
does answer.check_in
when self.tired=yes
say Tired, that's all. | Didn't sleep. | Long day. Longer night. | I could sleep standing.

rule s8a_checkin_low
does answer.check_in
when self.mood=low|sore
say Bit of a day, that's all. | Don't mind me. I'll come round. | Something on my mind. It'll keep.

rule s8a_checkin_hungry
does answer.check_in
when self.hungry=yes
say Hungry, mostly. | Haven't eaten. That'll be it. | Empty belly, sour face.

rule s8a_checkin_hurt
does answer.check_in
when self.injured=light|bad
say Took a knock. It'll mend. | Sore, that's all. | Just a hurt. Nothing broken.

rule s8a_checkin_bright
does answer.check_in
when self.mood=bright
tone light
say Never better, as it happens. | Me? I'm grand. | Not a care in the world, today.

## clarify: what one said, again

rule s8a_clarify_any
does clarify
say Never mind. It'll keep. | Oh, nothing. Forget it. | #pardon#, it's no matter. | It wasn't important. | I'll tell you later.

rule s8a_clarify_gossip
does clarify
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|life|news|newcomer
say #topic.subject#. You heard right. | #pardon# #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject#, I said. That's all.

rule s8a_clarify_prices
does clarify
when conv.topic=prices|price_cause
say Prices, I said. | The price of things. That's all. | #pardon#, it's all gone dear.

rule s8a_clarify_weather
does clarify
when conv.topic=weather|season
say The weather, I said. | Only the weather. | #pardon#, it's turned.

rule s8a_clarify_road
does clarify
when conv.topic=bandits|caravan|travel
say The road, I said. | The road. It's not safe. | About the wagons. That's all.

## extend: one more thing before parting (seldom: it weighs little beside taking the leave). What the one more thing is
## comes of the moment (plain.grammar's s8_extend: love to the house of a friend, the ice, the rain, the dark, the road),
## so no extend outranks the leave-taking it stands beside.

rule s8a_extend_any
does extend
weight 0.3
say #s8_extend# | #s8_extend#

## decline_apology: an apology not taken (seldom)

rule s8a_unforgiven_any
does decline_apology
weight 0.3
say #hedge#. I'm not ready to let it go yet. | Hm. Sorry's a start, I suppose. | Words are easy. We'll see, won't we. | I'll think about it. Not now, though.

rule s8a_unforgiven_sore
does decline_apology
when self.mood=sore
weight 0.4
say Not today. I'm too sore about it still. | You'll have to do better than that. | #hedge#, but it'll take more than sorry.

## answer.plan by trade (what a day holds for each)

rule s8a_plan_smith
does answer.plan
when self.job=smith
say The forge, as ever. | Nails, and more nails. | Mend what's broken, make what's wanted. | Keep the fire fed.

rule s8a_plan_crafter
does answer.plan
when self.job=crafter
say Whatever's on the bench. | Finish what I started yesterday. | Orders, if there are any.

rule s8a_plan_guard
does answer.plan
when self.job=guard|soldier
say My watch, then sleep. | Walk the rounds. Same as ever. | Keep the peace, if it'll be kept.

rule s8a_plan_healer
does answer.plan
when self.job=healer
say Whoever's sick, I'll see. | Rounds, and the herbs to dry. | Whatever ails the town today.

rule s8a_plan_priest
does answer.plan
when self.job=priest
say Prayers, then visiting. | The chapel wants sweeping, and the sick want seeing. | The Bright One's work.

rule s8a_plan_miner
does answer.plan
when self.job=miner
say Down the hole, same as yesterday. | Dig till the lamp says stop. | The seam, and then a bath.

rule s8a_plan_carter
does answer.plan
when self.job=carter
say Load up and go, if the road's fit. | Whatever wants carrying. | On the road by noon, I hope.

rule s8a_plan_labour
does answer.plan
when self.job=laborer|servant|woodcutter
say Fetch and carry, as ever. | Whatever I'm told. | Heavy work, then bed.

rule s8a_plan_scholar
does answer.plan
when self.job=scholar|official
say Papers, and more papers. | Reading, if they let me. | Counting, writing, sealing. The usual.

## answer.whereabouts by place and work

rule s8a_where_market
does answer.whereabouts
when here.place=market
say The market, mostly. | Round the stalls. | Here, haggling.

rule s8a_where_tavern
does answer.whereabouts
when here.place=tavern self.stage=adult|old
say Here, mostly, if I'm honest. | By this fire, more than I should be. | Nowhere a cup can't find me.

rule s8a_where_field
does answer.whereabouts
when self.job=farmer|herder
say Out in the fields. | With the beasts. | Up the top meadow, mostly.

rule s8a_where_water
does answer.whereabouts
when self.job=fisher|sailor
say On the water. | Down by the boats. | Out with the nets.
